<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech builder IPS 1996 net profit falls.</title>
<headline>Czech builder IPS 1996 net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech construction firm IPS a.s. preliminary unaudited net profit dipped to 91.2 million crowns in 1996 from 168.1 million in the previous year, according to filings with the Prague Stock Exchange obtained by Reuters on Thursday.  </p>
<p> Net profit (CZK million)  91.17   vs	   168.08</p>
<p> Gross profit		 111.82   vs	   242.20</p>
<p> Value of production    6,758.27   vs	 5,264.36</p>
<p> Total assets	     8,536.12   vs	 5,834.72</p>
<p> Basic capital	    1,437.04   vs	 1,300.36</p>
<p>NOTE. IPS is a Prague-based construction company. The results and comapratives were calculated according to Czech accounting standards and are unconsolidated. IPS shares are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
